{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c88cddde-d9ec-4df1-89bf-4cd0fc5db786","agentId":"ad3b2406af84b2e4d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, minimal grepping; one 400px-wide CDP screenshot allowed at the end for item 4 (cleanup via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py). Report under 100 words. You own: cuore/web/templates/job.html, jobs_routes.py, static/job.js, job.css, templates/bench.html, _vbar.html, _vtabs.html, static/cuore.css, cuore/tests/check_job_ux.py, check_bench_page.py (if present). Do not edit bridges or anything systems_*/tests_*/system.*.\n\n1. Job step 7 \"+ Add a hypothesis\" form reads ?system=<key>&codes=P0440,P0455 (and ?hypothesis=<id> to pre-select a card): pre-select the System select, pre-tick linked codes, expand the collapsed form, scroll to it. Also accept ?codes= on step 5 to highlight those codes' cards.\n2. Hypothesis pre-select in the step 6 result sheet: when several hypotheses are open, pre-select the one whose next_test matches the row (jobs_bridge already exposes next_test), else the one linked from \"Do it now\" (?hypothesis=), else none with the select labelled \"Choose a hypothesis…\" (not \"(none)\").\n3. Bench: in the \"links\" row add \"Tests\" -> /v/{vin}/tests and, when the verdict has a blocker or a top code, \"System: <label>\" -> /v/{vin}/systems/<key> of the top code's primary system (bench_bridge build_bench exposes codes with systems; if not, read the first code's systems via systems_bridge.systems_for_code in the route, not the template). Do not reorder Bench.\n4. The vehicle strip's \"…\" / More button is partly clipped at 400 px (reported earlier): fix in _vbar.html/_vtabs.html/cuore.css so at 400 px nothing is clipped and no horizontal scroll; verify with the screenshot and a bounding-rect check.\nTests: extend check_job_ux.py: ?system=evap&codes=P0440 pre-selects and pre-ticks; result sheet select default label; Bench page contains the Tests link and a /systems/ link. Run check_job_ux.py, check_jobs_page.py, check_screens.py, and the bench suite if present."},"uuid":"2deb8b4d-1617-4659-b69b-a8c71c3f02aa","timestamp":"2026-10-08T23:40:21.518Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
