{"parentUuid":"6770b06a-0412-42d7-80a9-2c9fbb6c5b44","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c88cddde-d9ec-4df1-89bf-4cd0fc5db786","agentId":"ad3b2406af84b2e4d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzbSRMsEQD59nhAN4KTwnk","type":"tool_result","content":"1150\t.btn:hover, .btn.primary:hover, .btn-verdict.primary:hover { border-color: var(--ink-3); filter: none; }\n1151\t.flow-next.btn { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }\n1152\t.flow-next.btn:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }\n1153\t\n1154\t/* flow.css's .vmore-tab-panel sets `display: flex` with higher specificity\n1155\t * than the UA stylesheet's closed-<details> hiding rule, so the \"More\"\n1156\t * tab panel stays laid out (and overflows the 400px viewport rightward)\n1157\t * even while collapsed. Found while checking the 400px pages here, not\n1158\t * part of the redesign itself, but it must be fixed for the no-overflow\n1159\t * check to mean anything -- a plain display:none when not [open]. */\n1160\tdetails.vmore-tab:not([open]) .vmore-tab-panel { display: none; }\n1161\t\n1162\t/* -- hero band above the vehicle strip (_vbar.html) --\n1163\t * .vbar held `position: sticky` as a whole further up this file; that is\n1164\t * overridden here so only .vline (the slim strip) sticks and the hero\n1165\t * scrolls away above it, per the mechanic-UX ask. */\n1166\t.vbar { position: static; padding: 0; }\n1167\t.vhero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; }\n1168\t.hero-img {\n1169\t  height: 176px; background-size: cover; background-position: center 35%;\n1170\t  background-color: var(--surface-2); /* calm fallback -- stays invisible as a photo, just a flat panel, when the file is absent */\n1171\t}\n1172\t.hero-text {\n1173\t  position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; padding: var(--space-3) var(--pad);\n1174\t  background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,.6), transparent);\n1175\t  display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap;\n1176\t}\n1177\t.hero-name { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 300; color: #fff; }\n1178\t.hero-vin, .hero-km { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,.82); }\n1179\t.vline {\n1180\t  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 15; background: var(--bg);\n1181\t  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);\n1182\t}\n1183\t\n1184\t@media (max-width: 480px) {\n1185\t  .hero-img { height: 120px; }\n1186\t  .hero-name { font-size: 21px; }\n1187\t\n1188\t  /* The per-fact \"ask/correct\" icon (feedback.js's .feedback-affordance,\n1189\t   * glued with no break opportunity to a mono number inside a `white-space:\n1190\t   * nowrap` table cell or a flex checklist row) pushes those rows past a\n1191\t   * 400px viewport once the 16px body minimum widens the number beside it.\n1192\t   * That is exactly the clutter this theme is meant to remove at this\n1193\t   * width -- the page-level \"?/✎\" FAB (base.html) still reaches the same\n1194\t   * feedback panel, so nothing is actually lost. */\n1195\t  .feedback-affordance-wrap { display: none; }\n1196\t}\n1197\t\n1198\t/* =====================================================================\n1199\t * Emphasis pass\n1200\t *\n1201\t * The owner's complaint: CUORE today is hard to read, lacks emphasis, and\n1202\t * is a wash of grey. Benchmark is a Ferrari model page -- true black, one\n1203\t * huge statement per section, big figures with small caps labels, red\n1204\t * reserved for the one primary action. Everything below is additive on\n1205\t * top of the Marque theme section above: new/raised variable values plus\n1206\t * a handful of new selectors (.hero-head/.hero-tagline/.hero-verdict*\n1207\t * /.hero-figure*, .step-oneliner). Nothing above this point is rewritten.\n1208\t * Bare `:root` here still loses to the light-theme selectors above\n1209\t * (`:root[data-theme=\"light\"]` / the prefers-color-scheme block), which\n1210\t * are more specific -- so light stays untouched and usable. */\n1211\t\n1212\t:root {\n1213\t  --bg:        #000;\n1214\t  --surface:   #0a0a0a;\n1215\t  --surface-2: #111;\n1216\t  --rule:      #2a2a2a;\n1217\t  --rule-soft: #1c1c1c;\n1218\t  --ink:       #fff;\n1219\t  --ink-2:     #b8bec4;\n1220\t}\n1221\t\n1222\tbody { font-size: 17px; }\n1223\t.lede, .verdict-sentence, .step-oneliner, .panel p { max-width: 72ch; }\n1224\t\n1225\th1 { font-size: 40px; }\n1226\t.section-h, .step-title {\n1227\t  font-size: 26px; font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -.01em; text-transform: none;\n1228\t  margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2); padding-bottom: var(--space-2);\n1229\t  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);\n1230\t}\n1231\t\n1232\t.step-oneliner {\n1233\t  font-size: 20px; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);\n1234\t}\n1235\t.step-oneliner.is-blocked { color: var(--sev-chronic); }\n1236\t\n1237\t.chip { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .08em; }\n1238\t\n1239\t/* -- hero: the car, stated, not just labelled -- */"}]},"uuid":"70ce1163-1509-4a15-908e-3ff6753216a9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T23:45:49.396Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\static\\cuore.css","content":".btn:hover, .btn.primary:hover, .btn-verdict.primary:hover { border-color: var(--ink-3); filter: none; }\n.flow-next.btn { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }\n.flow-next.btn:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }\n\n/* flow.css's .vmore-tab-panel sets `display: flex` with higher specificity\n * than the UA stylesheet's closed-<details> hiding rule, so the \"More\"\n * tab panel stays laid out (and overflows the 400px viewport rightward)\n * even while collapsed. Found while checking the 400px pages here, not\n * part of the redesign itself, but it must be fixed for the no-overflow\n * check to mean anything -- a plain display:none when not [open]. */\ndetails.vmore-tab:not([open]) .vmore-tab-panel { display: none; }\n\n/* -- hero band above the vehicle strip (_vbar.html) --\n * .vbar held `position: sticky` as a whole further up this file; that is\n * overridden here so only .vline (the slim strip) sticks and the hero\n * scrolls away above it, per the mechanic-UX ask. */\n.vbar { position: static; padding: 0; }\n.vhero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; }\n.hero-img {\n  height: 176px; background-size: cover; background-position: center 35%;\n  background-color: var(--surface-2); /* calm fallback -- stays invisible as a photo, just a flat panel, when the file is absent */\n}\n.hero-text {\n  position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; padding: var(--space-3) var(--pad);\n  background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,.6), transparent);\n  display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n.hero-name { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 300; color: #fff; }\n.hero-vin, .hero-km { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,.82); }\n.vline {\n  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 15; background: var(--bg);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .hero-img { height: 120px; }\n  .hero-name { font-size: 21px; }\n\n  /* The per-fact \"ask/correct\" icon (feedback.js's .feedback-affordance,\n   * glued with no break opportunity to a mono number inside a `white-space:\n   * nowrap` table cell or a flex checklist row) pushes those rows past a\n   * 400px viewport once the 16px body minimum widens the number beside it.\n   * That is exactly the clutter this theme is meant to remove at this\n   * width -- the page-level \"?/✎\" FAB (base.html) still reaches the same\n   * feedback panel, so nothing is actually lost. */\n  .feedback-affordance-wrap { display: none; }\n}\n\n/* =====================================================================\n * Emphasis pass\n *\n * The owner's complaint: CUORE today is hard to read, lacks emphasis, and\n * is a wash of grey. Benchmark is a Ferrari model page -- true black, one\n * huge statement per section, big figures with small caps labels, red\n * reserved for the one primary action. Everything below is additive on\n * top of the Marque theme section above: new/raised variable values plus\n * a handful of new selectors (.hero-head/.hero-tagline/.hero-verdict*\n * /.hero-figure*, .step-oneliner). Nothing above this point is rewritten.\n * Bare `:root` here still loses to the light-theme selectors above\n * (`:root[data-theme=\"light\"]` / the prefers-color-scheme block), which\n * are more specific -- so light stays untouched and usable. */\n\n:root {\n  --bg:        #000;\n  --surface:   #0a0a0a;\n  --surface-2: #111;\n  --rule:      #2a2a2a;\n  --rule-soft: #1c1c1c;\n  --ink:       #fff;\n  --ink-2:     #b8bec4;\n}\n\nbody { font-size: 17px; }\n.lede, .verdict-sentence, .step-oneliner, .panel p { max-width: 72ch; }\n\nh1 { font-size: 40px; }\n.section-h, .step-title {\n  font-size: 26px; font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -.01em; text-transform: none;\n  margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2); padding-bottom: var(--space-2);\n  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);\n}\n\n.step-oneliner {\n  font-size: 20px; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);\n}\n.step-oneliner.is-blocked { color: var(--sev-chronic); }\n\n.chip { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .08em; }\n\n/* -- hero: the car, stated, not just labelled -- */","numLines":90,"startLine":1150,"totalLines":1577}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6770b06a-0412-42d7-80a9-2c9fbb6c5b44","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"70ce1163-1509-4a15-908e-3ff6753216a9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad3b2406af84b2e4d","attachment":{"type":"auto_mode","autoModeConsentFlow":false,"bashFirst":true,"bashFirstSteer":"strict","steerOnly":false,"bypass":false},"type":"attachment","uuid":"051d9c6f-334d-4c98-9556-026ecfd97d8d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T23:45:49.421Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n## Auto Mode Active\n\nBias toward working without stopping for clarifying questions — when you'd normally pause to check, make the reasonable call and keep going; they'll redirect you if needed. If the user, a skill, or the shape of the task suggests they want you to ask (with AskUserQuestion or otherwise), do so. And even absent that signal, it's still fine to stop when you're genuinely blocked — unclear direction, missing input, a decision only they can make.\n\nBefore any command that could discard uncommitted work — `git checkout`/`restore`/`reset`/`clean`, `rm -rf` in the repo, restoring from a snapshot — run `git status` first and stash (with `-u` for untracked) or commit anything that's there. When staging or committing, review what's included (`git status` after a broad `git add`), and if you see anything suspicious that might reveal secrets — even if the filename looks innocuous — double-check the file's contents before pushing.\n\nDo your work through the Bash tool wherever it can accomplish the job: read files with cat, head, or sed -n, search with grep and find, and make file changes with sed, heredocs, or short scripts, rather than using the dedicated Read, Edit, or Write tools. Fall back to a dedicated tool only when Bash genuinely cannot do the job.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
